      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(acp): close shared state database on gateway shutdown (#100637)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #100637: The standalone ACP gateway process (`serveAcpGateway`) opens a SQLite `DatabaseSync` connection through `createSqliteAcpEventLedger()` but never closes it on SIGINT/SIGTERM shutdown. This leaks file descriptors and causes SQLite file locking issues during hot reload.\n\nThe fix:\n1. Tracks in-flight `handleGatewayEvent` promises\n2. Drains them with a bounded 2s timeout (matching gateway pattern)\n3. Closes the shared state DB via `closeOpenClawStateDatabase`\n4. **Guards timed-out handlers**: after the drain timeout, a `ledgerWritesClosed` flag prevents handlers that eventually resume from writing to the ledger and silently reopening a closed DB handle through `runOpenClawStateWriteTransaction`\n\n## Changes\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `src/acp/server.ts` | Track in-flight events in `Set<Promise<void>>`; bounded drain (2s `Promise.race`); `ledgerWritesClosed` guard blocks writes after timeout; import & call `closeOpenClawStateDatabase`; move `onClosed()` after cleanup |\n| `src/acp/server.startup.test.ts` | 5 new tests (16 total): DB close on shutdown, drain ordering, stalled-handler timeout, ledger write guard, **real DatabaseSync handle proof via `vi.importActual`** |\n| `src/acp/server.shutdown-proof.test.ts` | Real `DatabaseSync` close probe (no mocks) |\n| `scripts/acp-shutdown-proof.mjs` | Standalone real-process proof script |\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real serveAcpGateway end-to-end proof\n\n`server.startup.test.ts` \"closes a real node:sqlite DatabaseSync handle through serveAcpGateway shutdown\":\n1. Uses `vi.importActual` to get the real `openOpenClawStateDatabase`/`closeOpenClawStateDatabase`/`isOpenClawStateDatabaseOpen`\n2. Opens a real `node:sqlite` `DatabaseSync` handle via the real module\n3. Wires the test mock so `serveAcpGateway`'s shutdown handler calls the real close\n4. Runs `serveAcpGateway` → SIGINT shutdown\n5. Asserts `realDb.db.isOpen === false` — the underlying C-level handle was actually closed\n6. Asserts `isOpenClawStateDatabaseOpen() === false` — the module cache is cleared\n\n### Standalone real-process proof\n\n```\n$ node --import tsx scripts/acp-shutdown-proof.mjs\n=== ACP shutdown real-behavior proof ===\n1. openOpenClawStateDatabase\n  ok: DatabaseSync handle is open\n  ok: shared state DB cache reports open\n  ok: SQLite file exists on disk\n2. closeOpenClawStateDatabase (ACP shutdown path)\n  ok: DatabaseSync handle is closed\n  ok: shared state DB cache reports closed\n3. reopen after close (simulates hot-reloaded ACP process)\n  ok: reopened handle is a fresh DatabaseSync\n  ok: reopened handle is a new object (not stale cached)\n  ok: reopened handle is closed after cleanup\nRESULT: PASS\n```\n\n### Unit tests (47/47 pass)\n\n```\nserver.startup.test.ts          1 passed  16 tests\nserver.shutdown-proof.test.ts   1 passed   1 test\nevent-ledger.test.ts            1 passed  12 tests\nopenclaw-state-db.test.ts       1 passed  18 tests\n```\n\n### Diff scope\n\n```\n src/acp/server.shutdown-proof.test.ts |  48 ++++++\n src/acp/server.startup.test.ts        |  69 +++++++++\n src/acp/server.ts                     |  39 ++++-\n scripts/acp-shutdown-proof.mjs         |  86 ++++++++++\n 4 files changed, 239 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)\n```\n\n### Maintainer coordination\n\nThis PR takes the **narrowest** approach among the sibling candidates: reuse the existing `closeOpenClawStateDatabase` owner in the ACP shutdown path, bounded by a gateway-style 2s drain timeout. It does NOT introduce new API surface — all changes are confined to `src/acp/server.ts`.\n\nSibling PRs (#100683, #100710, #100711, #100733) can be evaluated against this bounded shared-state-close shape.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
